„­bible_version£KJV¤book§chapter	¨sections˜…¤book§chapter	«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‹Oh that my head were waters, and mine eyes a fountain of tears, that I might weep day and night for the slain of the daughter of my people!¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ­Oh that I had in the wilderness a lodging place of wayfaring men; that I might leave my people, and go from them! for they be all adulterers, an assembly of treacherous men.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter	«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙµAnd they bend their tongues like their bow for lies: but they are not valiant for the truth upon the earth; for they proceed from evil to evil, and they know not me, saith the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŸTake ye heed every one of his neighbour, and trust ye not in any brother: for every brother will utterly supplant, and every neighbour will walk with slanders.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¢And they will deceive every one his neighbour, and will not speak the truth: they have taught their tongue to speak lies, and weary themselves to commit iniquity.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙbThine habitation is in the midst of deceit; through deceit they refuse to know me, saith the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter	«first_verseªlast_verse	¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙTherefore thus saith the LORD of hosts, Behold, I will melt them, and try them; for how shall I do for the daughter of my people?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ’Their tongue is as an arrow shot out; it speaketh deceit: one speaketh peaceably to his neighbour with his mouth, but in heart he layeth his wait.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙoShall I not visit them for these things? saith the LORD: shall not my soul be avenged on such a nation